{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$c=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r3\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$i=686;$i -le 716;$i++){Write-Output (($i+1).ToString()+'\"':'+\"'$c[$i])}; for($i=928;$i -le 962;$i++){Write-Output (($i+1).ToString()+'\"':'+\"'$c[$i])}'","aggregated_output":"687:  law (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:184-186).\r\n688:- META survives by construction (:1403-1413) -- exactly how `meta.visual_style`,\r\n689:  `meta.freeze_*`, `meta.gap_audit_*` persist today.\r\n690:\r\n691:### 5.2 Write path\r\n692:\r\n693:1. Preconditions (ALL fail-closed): `meta.visual_style == \"dynamic_story\"`;\r\n694:   `meta.cleanup_locked is True`; `meta.freeze_verdict` in\r\n695:   `{frozen_clean, frozen_with_warns}` (`needs_full_rerun` refuses,\r\n696:   nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-811); non-empty `lines`/`cast`.\r\n697:2. Build `DirectionSourceV1` and compute `source_sha256` (2.5).\r\n698:3. Context preflight for P-A and P-B, worst-case repair envelope included (4.4).\r\n699:   Overflow raises HERE, before any generation.\r\n700:4. P-A via `structured_call` on the creative slot with the must-fit slot_fn\r\n701:   (4.2, 4.3, 4.5). Then P-B, batched.\r\n702:5. Assemble the pack (safety base + authored `look`); validate the whole vd-1\r\n703:   artifact: embedded pack through `_validate_row`\r\n704:   (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:184+), evidence resolution, geometry lint,\r\n705:   whitelist collision, shots coverage.\r\n706:6. REBUILD `DirectionSourceV1` from the live ledger and refuse to stamp on any\r\n707:   delta (`content_mutations` must be 0).\r\n708:7. Seal (`semantic_sha256`, `artifact_sha256`), stamp `meta.visual_direction` on\r\n709:   the wire ledger, and persist via\r\n710:   `stamp_durable(meta_updates={\"visual_direction\": ...})`\r\n711:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:408-422). Before stamping durably, verify\r\n712:   `peek_ledger()`'s episode_id matches the wire ledger's (:372-397) -- the\r\n713:   process singleton can be stale (r2 codex S6).\r\n714:8. `finally`: LLM teardown (5.5).\r\n715:\r\n716:### 5.3 Read path: `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> VisualStyle`\r\n717:\r\n929:\r\n930:## 8. Code / workflow surfaces -- ALL \"not implemented\"\r\n931:\r\n932:1. **NEW node `nodes/otr_dynamic_story_direction.py`\r\n933:   (`OTR_DynamicStoryDirection`)**. `INPUT_TYPES`: required `script_json`\r\n934:   (STRING, forceInput), optional `gate_in` (STRING, forceInput, opaque).\r\n935:   `RETURN_TYPES/RETURN_NAMES`: `(\"STRING\",\"STRING\",\"STRING\")` /\r\n936:   `(\"patched_ledger_json\", \"direction_report\", \"done\")` -- the CastLock/ShotLock\r\n937:   idiom (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:966-969). `direction_report` is the operator's\r\n938:   only human-readable surface for a taste feature; `done` is the standard opaque\r\n939:   ordering STRING (ShotLock's own `done` ships UNWIRED, `links: []`, in the live\r\n940:   canonical file). Both ship UNWIRED in v1 -- stated explicitly so the link audit\r\n941:   expects nothing. `FUNCTION`, `CATEGORY`, `VALIDATE_INPUTS`. Zero widgets ->\r\n942:   `widgets_values: []`.\r\n943:2. **Registration in the LITERAL `_NODE_MODULES` dict in `__init__.py`**\r\n944:   (:119-325; one tuple entry supplies BOTH the class mapping and the display\r\n945:   name, written by the loader loop at :362-363). **NOT** via\r\n946:   `nodes/_otr_class_registry.py`: the canonical-workflow contract test builds its\r\n947:   node-class mappings by AST-parsing the literal `_NODE_MODULES` dict\r\n948:   (tests/test_workflow_contract_validation.py:41) and never executes the class-\r\n949:   registry merge (__init__.py:335-349) -- a registry-only node is INVISIBLE to\r\n950:   the workflow gate.\r\n951:3. **Workflow JSON delta (same change as the code, CLAUDE.md section 0).**\r\n952:   Node id **96**, new link id **284**. Add `[284, 62, 1, 96, 0, \"STRING\"]`;\r\n953:   REPOINT the existing links rather than renumbering:\r\n954:   `[252, 96, 0, 90, 0, \"STRING\"]` and `[255, 96, 0, 89, 0, \"STRING\"]`. Node 62\r\n955:   `outputs[1].links` becomes `[16, 231, 232, 233, 284]` (the audio trio + the\r\n956:   signal-lost read STAY on the raw freeze json). New node `outputs[0].links` =\r\n957:   `[252, 255]`. `last_node_id = 96`, `last_link_id = 284`. `widgets_values: []`.\r\n958:   r3 owns the FULL record (pos/size/order/properties) and the test-pin sweep.\r\n959:4. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction.py`** (lazy; pydantic + stdlib): the two typed\r\n960:   models, `DirectionSourceV1` + the canonical hasher (shared by writer and\r\n961:   readers), evidence resolution, geometry lint, pack assembly, the fail-closed\r\n962:   matrix, `resolve_visual_direction(ledger)`.\r\n963:5. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction_prompts.py`**: the P-A and P-B base prompts,\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
