{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_88","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$c=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r3\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$i=715;$i -le 750;$i++){Write-Output (($i+1).ToString()+'\"':'+\"'$c[$i])}; for($i=868;$i -le 884;$i++){Write-Output (($i+1).ToString()+'\"':'+\"'$c[$i])}'","aggregated_output":"716:### 5.3 Read path: `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> VisualStyle`\r\n717:\r\n718:`get_visual_style(meta)` cannot enforce the staleness matrix -- it never sees the\r\n719:arrays (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390). ONE new ledger-aware function\r\n720:validates the artifact and returns the assembled `VisualStyle`. It is called at\r\n721:each consumer ENTRY and the result is threaded down the existing `style=`\r\n722:parameters -- the resolve-once contract already in force\r\n723:(nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609).\r\n724:\r\n725:Three consumer entries, and **two of them need a signature change** (r2):\r\n726:\r\n727:- **MetaBrief:** `generate()` holds the parsed `led`\r\n728:  (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:2137-2144) -- it resolves there and\r\n729:  passes the result down. `derive_image_prompts` gains a `style=None` (and a\r\n730:  shots-note index) parameter instead of calling `_resolve_style(meta)` itself\r\n731:  (:1570-1574, :1609). The threaded style must reach EVERY branch that composes\r\n732:  a prompt -- portrait, character scene, radio-host, mesh fodder, plate,\r\n733:  still_word -- not just the still_word mood seam.\r\n734:- **ShotLock:** holds the whole `led` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040); resolves\r\n735:  ONCE before the beat loop, outside the fail-soft block (7.2).\r\n736:- **render_driver:** resolves once in the episode entry and threads the result\r\n737:  through the shot-request builders instead of calling `get_visual_style(meta)`\r\n738:  at :1248.\r\n739:\r\n740:REJECTED alternative (r1): reading the `peek_ledger()` process singleton inside\r\n741:`get_visual_style` -- consumers operate on the WIRE ledger, and the singleton can\r\n742:lag or be absent in that seam.\r\n743:\r\n744:The dynamic `VisualStyle` instance NEVER enters the module pack cache (`_STYLES`,\r\n745:nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:170, 355-359); it is built per resolve from the\r\n746:artifact.\r\n747:\r\n748:### 5.4 Look authority on the dynamic lane (both lanes)\r\n749:\r\n750:Today the brief outranks the pack for the era tail\r\n751:(nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:356-370, 401, 414, 428) -- correct for named\r\n869:  (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609) puts the SAME instance behind\r\n870:  every prompt.\r\n871:- `shots[].subject_note/mood` are ADDITIVE clauses appended at the same seam the\r\n872:  beat mood token uses today (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1004-1008);\r\n873:  they can never replace pack-level fields, are capped at 240 chars, and are\r\n874:  linted against the safety-base `forbidden_terms` + the Python geometry\r\n875:  vocabulary at validation time.\r\n876:- On the dynamic lane MetaBrief's consumption of `shots[]` is MANDATORY (an\r\n877:  authored note that is never consumed is dead scope; a `line_id` present in\r\n878:  `shots[]` but absent from the ledger fails validation).\r\n879:- Engine-safety continuity is structural: talking/mouth/motion/subject/typography\r\n880:  fields come from the vetted base (2.4), so no per-episode LLM output can\r\n881:  degrade lip-sync or motion behavior. `render_driver`'s `motion_registers` reads\r\n882:  therefore never vary with LLM output.\r\n883:\r\n884:### 7.5 Replay, reruns, and the reroll cut\r\n885:\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
