{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"agent_message","text":"VERDICT: no. Core sequencing, repair, context-budget, durability, consumer, and canonical-workflow contracts remain unimplementable or internally contradictory.\n\nMUST-FIX BEFORE BUILD:\n\n1. [§5.2, §8.1–8.3] The direction pass is neither gated on successful freeze teardown nor ordered before audio work. §5.2 omits `freeze_unload_ok`; §8 leaves `done` unwired even though the first voice node exposes `gate_in` specifically for ordering. [ASSUMPTION] Independent fan-outs have no guaranteed execution order without an edge. Require `meta.freeze_unload_ok is True` before `request_slot`; emit `done` only after successful direction teardown; add `[285,96,2,81,2,\"STRING\"]`, set node-96 out[2] to `[285]`, node-81 `gate_in` to 285, and `last_link_id=285`. Preserve nodes 81/82/83’s raw-freeze `script_json` links. `input.md:693-714,932-957`; `nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:452-492`; `nodes/_otr_voice_node_common.py:295-302`; `workflows/otr_canonical.json:1`.\n\n2. [§4.1, §4.5 / Lessons 3–4] The selected parser silently rewrites authored content. `parse_validate_tolerant` truncates overlong strings at any depth and accepts the result, contradicting the plan’s claim that authored visual text advances to repair. Add a strict/no-clamp mode to `structured_call` and require it for both vd schemas; every overlength value must enter typed repair or fail closed. `input.md:510-518,662-671`; `nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:391-438,489-543`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:38-64`.\n\n3. [§4.5, §9.1] Wrong-depth repair is wired to impossible examples. P-A has no legal top-level `shots`, P-B has no `motifs`, and bare nested `evidence: [str]` cannot become a keyed `{evidence,kind}` entry without inventing data. Also, if a repair factory returns a model that later fails `post_validator`, `structured_call` has no repair prompt cached and exhausts instead of falling through. Permit deterministic relocation only within the same pass when exactly one candidate—or multiple byte-identical candidates—has a unique verbatim destination; validate the complete contract inside the factory and otherwise return typed-repair messages. `input.md:665-671,1003-1007`; `nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:737-811`; `nodes/_otr_original_codex56sol.py:583-645`; `docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:469-487`.\n\n4. [§2.5, §3.3, §4.4 / Lesson 1] The source and row contracts are not closed. `DirectionSourceV1` claims to be the sole prompt/hash/evidence DTO, but P-A uses an unspecified truncated projection and P-B uses a different batch projection. It also duplicates `story_brief_terms` under both `meta` and `brief`, while blanket `null -> \"\"` is invalid for Boolean `skip` and list-valued brief fields. Define exact typed projections and normalization defaults—or pass the full DTO—and require aggregate P-B set equality: exactly one ordered row per non-skipped line, no omissions, and each row must cite its own `line:<line_id>`. `input.md:397-421,498-500,601-620`; `nodes/_otr_story_brief.py:219-226`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:7-21`.\n\n5. [§4.3–4.4, §5.2 / Lesson 5] Preflight order cannot execute as written. P-B needs P-A’s authored look, yet step 3 demands tokenizing both prompts before P-A runs; no `request_slot`/cache entry exists before that step. Further, fifteen legal 240-character notes can exceed the 900-token P-B reservation before JSON/evidence overhead. Load inside the teardown-protected region, preflight P-A, use a schema-maximum P-B bound before any generation, run P-A, then exactly preflight each real P-B batch. Derive batch size and output reservation from measured maxima rather than fixing 15/900. `input.md:611-628,691-714`; `nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:790-815,940-1026`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:66-75`.\n\n6. [§4.2–4.4, §9.2] Provider propagation is incomplete. OpenRouter, Comfy, Google, and GGUF entries lack an HF tokenizer, so the proposed shared must-fit helper cannot measure them. OpenRouter/Comfy also raise P-B’s requested 900 tokens to a 1024-token floor and may override temperature/caps, while the receipt hard-codes local `do_sample/top_p` semantics. Google is advertised for qualification but has no branch in `make_constrained_generate_fn`. Define one provider-effective configuration/counting interface used by preflight, invocation, and receipt; add Google schema-response support or explicitly exclude Google from constrained configurations. `input.md:303-308,556-560,587-591,1069-1078`; `nodes/_otr_openrouter_backend.py:905-920,958-985`; `nodes/_otr_comfy_backend.py:426-438,472-480`; `nodes/_otr_google_api/llm.py:115-121,145-162`; `nodes/_otr_gguf_backend.py:393-402`; `nodes/_otr_constrained_generate.py:196-244`.\n\n7. [§3.1, §5.3, §7.4] `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> VisualStyle` cannot supply the mandatory shots index or semantic digest. This forces consumers either to reread unvalidated `meta` or ignore fields. Return a typed resolved bundle containing `style`, `shots_by_line_id`, `semantic_sha256`, and validated artifact metadata. Define the exact per-kind consumption matrix before `prompt_hash`: character scene, ordinary scene, still-word, mesh subject, and subject-free background plate cannot all accept the same appended clause. Also state explicitly whether ShotLock/render_driver consume per-line notes or whether `shots[]` is still-only. `input.md:716-738,869-878`; `nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1903-2083`; `nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:499-647`; `nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py:1220-1248`.\n\n8. [§2.3, §4.5 / Lessons 4 and 13] `attempt_journal` has no producer interface. `structured_call` returns only the accepted model and exposes no rung/outcome callback; a wrapper can hash raw calls but cannot know parse failures, deterministic repair, or validation reasons. Add an internal attempt-event sink/result carrying pass, batch ID/source-line IDs, rung, outcome, reason, effective config, and prompt/response or normalized-result hashes. Persist bounded accepted-state receipts, not rejected raw outputs. `input.md:309-312,673-675`; `nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:551-568,662-823`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:167-177`.\n\n9. [§5.2, §5.5, §6] Lifecycle order contradicts itself. Step 7 seals and durably stamps before step 8 teardown, while §5.5 requires an unload receipt and post-teardown serialization. Follow the cascade pattern: generate/validate, unload in `finally`, persist a failed receipt then raise on teardown failure, and only after successful teardown seal, persist, serialize, and emit `done`. MetaBrief has no ledger output, so either specify its dynamic-only `stamp_durable` path or remove that durable-receipt claim. New receipts must be dynamic-only to preserve named-pack ledger byte identity. `input.md:708-714,778-785,809-818`; `nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:422-492`; `nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:2099-2187`.\n\n10. [§7.5–7.6, §8.11–8.13] The audit chain is not durable. Video `creative` sidecars currently exist only on the wire, and image rows store `prompt_hash` but not the claimed prompt. Cache hits clone old rows and replace provenance, so they can retain or erase stale direction attribution. On the dynamic lane, fail-loud persist the ShotLock video section; store the current prompt and direction binding on both image hit and miss paths and in the still manifest. Scope attribution to the current v1 artifact unless digest-keyed artifact history is added later. `input.md:902-924,1110-1112`; `nodes/otr_video_render_batch.py:277-283`; `nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:603-643,771-779`.\n\n11. [§8.1–8.3, §9.1 / Lesson 7] The workflow delta promises a “FULL record” but omits it. Supply literal node-96 values for `pos`, `size`, `flags`, `order`, `mode`, complete inputs/outputs, slot indexes, localized names, title, properties, colors, and widget vector; state exact `CATEGORY`, `FUNCTION`, `OUTPUT_NODE`, `VALIDATE_INPUTS`, and display name. Add a topology test pinning registration and `62:1 -> 96:0 -> {89:0,90:0}`, plus the direction-to-audio ordering edge above. Run `OTR_WorkflowValidator`, JSON round-trip, live `INPUT_TYPES`/widget audit, and link reconciliation. `input.md:932-958`; `CLAUDE.md:9-23`; `tests/test_workflow_contract_validation.py:41-98`; `tests/test_google_video_sfx_workflow.py:35-41`.\n\n12. [§2.2–2.3, §4.1 / Lessons 1, 2, 11] The five representations and provenance grammar still disagree. There are two schemas but only one worked fixture; motif/clue evidence is duplicated inline and in `field_evidence`; artifact re-keying is unspecified; `era_cues` lacks evidence; and dotted-path keys are simultaneously required and globally forbidden. More importantly, ID existence alone now fails Lesson 11’s semantic-provenance rule. Provide complete separate P-A/P-B fixtures, exact field bounds, one evidence authority and final key grammar, and validated factual anchors carrying source field/start/end/exact quote rather than bare IDs. `input.md:241-288,335-339,510-532`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:23-35,142-153`.\n\n13. [§6, §9.1 / Lesson 12] The test plan does not prove channel isolation. Its named-pack before/after baseline does not run the same mocked story twice while changing only `visual_style`. Add a capture test comparing every pre-freeze story-model message for `sci_fi_radio` versus `dynamic_story`; only the post-freeze direction lane and selector receipt may differ. `input.md:1017-1022`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:155-165`.\n\nSHOULD-FIX:\n\n1. [§8.1] State the caching policy explicitly. [ASSUMPTION] If identical frozen JSON can reach node 96 directly, no `IS_CHANGED` means stochastic/remote generation and `created_utc` may be served from cache. Either make immutable-per-source caching intentional and test it, or add an `IS_CHANGED` contract. `nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3033-3038`; `nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:269-272`.\n\n2. [§8.1] `direction_report` is described as the only operator-readable surface but is unwired and the node is not specified as an output node. Log or durably expose it, wire a sink, or remove the observability claim. `input.md:936-941`.\n\n3. [§9.2] Resolve one concrete cloud model and its auth/rate policy before qualification. If Google remains eligible, distinguish transient 429 rate limiting from terminal quota and add bounded `Retry-After`/backoff or batch pacing; current Google code treats every 429 as terminal. `nodes/_otr_google_api/client.py:81-92,263-279`.\n\n4. [§2.3, §7.5] Separate “generated under” from “currently compatible with” attribution before future re-direction. A prompt-identical cache hit cannot truthfully identify an overwritten historical artifact unless history is retained.\n\nOPTIONAL / NICE-TO-HAVE:\n\n- Record per-batch measured input, repair-envelope, and effective-output tokens in the sprint receipt.\n- Add a compact UI diff showing named-pack versus dynamic prompt tails; keep the durable artifact authoritative.\n\nCUT THESE:\n\n1. [§8.1] Cut the unwired optional `gate_in` on node 96. No producer or sequencing use is defined, and the required ordering edge is outbound `done -> node81.gate_in`.\n\n2. [§8.1] Cut `direction_report` as a node output if it remains unwired; the durable artifact plus normal logging already cover diagnostics.\n\n3. [§2.3, §7.3] Cut persisted `story_binding.content_mutations`. Keep the before/after hash check, but refuse the stamp on nonzero; every successfully stored artifact would otherwise carry the redundant constant `0`.\n\n4. [§7.5–7.6] Cut the “after later re-direction” provenance promise from v1. Reroll/revision is explicitly out of scope, and satisfying that promise now requires artifact history plus dual cache attribution."}}
